kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[1]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,tui53,"always-on-status-line","The TUI MUST render a fixed always-present status line between the mutable streaming line and the bottom input panel, occupying exactly one row every frame (idle and streaming). The status line MUST use a three-segment layout (left left-aligned, center centered, right right-aligned) as an extensible skeleton so future status items (token count, elapsed time, context-window usage) can be added to a segment without changing widget render logic. The spinner glyph MUST sit fixed at the start of the left segment while streaming (animated by the existing Tick-driven spinner_idx). The left segment also shows a human activity label (Working while streaming with no tool, Running {tool} while a tool executes, Ready while idle). The center segment shows the current ReAct iteration count from TurnStart while streaming. The right segment shows the current model name from ModelSelect. The status line MUST be data-driven: TuiApp exposes a status_segments() accessor and the widget renders segments by alignment without matching business state itself. The spinner widget MUST be wired into this line (not merely present as an unwired component). The SPINNER frame constant MUST have a single source of truth. Evidence: the Spinner widget existed but was never rendered (6415f48 added it as a future building block); TuiApp already tracked spinner_idx and tool_status but did not surface them; user requested a fixed status row below the streaming line and above the input, extensible for future items.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[4]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui53,"status-line-present-idle","the TUI is idle with no turn streaming","the tail frame is rendered","a status line row is present showing the model name (right) and a Ready label (left) and no spinner"
  tui53,"status-line-streaming-spinner","a turn is streaming with no tool running","the tail frame is rendered over several ticks","the status line shows an animated spinner glyph at the left segment start and a Working label and the turn count (center) and the model name (right)"
  tui53,"status-line-tool-running","a ToolExecutionStart has occurred during a turn","the tail frame is rendered","the status line left segment shows the running tool name (e.g. Running bash) in place of Working"
  tui53,"status-line-three-segment-extensible","the status line source is inspected","the layout structure is read","it renders a left a center and a right segment by alignment and the widget does not match business state directly (it consumes a segments accessor)"
